Problem description
- There are $$n$$ locations indexed by $$i \in \mathcal{N}=\{1,2,\dots,n\}$$, and one designated depot location $$r \in \mathcal{N}$$ where the tour must both start and end.
- The travel cost between any two locations is given by a symmetric distance matrix $$D \in \mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}^{n \times n}$$, where $$D_{ij}$$ is the distance from location $$i$$ to location $$j$$.
- The planning goal is to determine a single minimum-distance closed tour that visits all locations exactly once and returns to the depot.
- The route must begin at the depot $$r$$, visit every other location exactly one time, and end at the same depot $$r$$.
- The tour must not split into disconnected partial cycles; all visited locations must belong to one continuous visiting order.
- Distances are additive over consecutive travel legs, and the objective is to minimize the total travel distance of the full tour.
- A solution is represented by:
  - a tour sequence $$\pi$$ listing the visited locations in order, with $$\pi_1=r$$ and $$\pi_{n+1}=r$$;
  - or equivalently a set of directed travel decisions $$x_{ij}$$ indicating whether the route goes directly from location $$i$$ to location $$j$$;
  - optionally, auxiliary ordering variables $$u_i$$ for enforcing a valid single tour without subtours.

Input Format
{
  "n": "number of locations, represented symbolically as $$n$$",
  "r": "depot index, represented symbolically as $$r$$",
  "D": {
    "type": "symmetric distance matrix",
    "shape": "$$n \\times n$$",
    "meaning": "$$D_{ij}$$ is the travel distance between locations $$i$$ and $$j$$, with $$D_{ij}=D_{ji}$$"
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "tour": {
    "type": "ordered list of location indices",
    "shape": "$$n+1$$",
    "meaning": "a minimum-distance visiting order that starts at $$r$$, visits each location exactly once, and ends at $$r$$"
  },
  "total_distance": {
    "type": "scalar",
    "meaning": "the total travel distance of the returned tour"
  }
}

Example(s)

Input 1
{
  "n":  "7",
  "r":  "1",
  "D": [
    ["0", "86", "49", "57", "31", "69", "50"],
    ["86", "0", "68", "79", "93", "24", "5"],
    ["49", "68", "0", "16", "7", "72", "67"],
    ["57", "79", "16", "0", "90", "69", "1"],
    ["31", "93", "7", "90", "0", "86", "59"],
    ["69", "24", "72", "69", "86", "0", "81"],
    ["50", "5", "67", "1", "59", "81", "0"]
  ]
}
